values ('b8c9d0e1-2f3a-4c02-9f12-2d3e4f5a6b22', 'site-planning-and-landscape', 'Site Planning and Landscape', 'Students learn that site is not background scenery; it is a set of physical, ecological, social, infrastructural, legal, and experiential forces that shape architecture. The course covers inventory and mapping, landform and accessible grading, water-sensitive design, living systems and planting, program and circulation, hardscape and outdoor comfort, urban and regional systems, regulation and feasibility, climate and equity, representation, and community, synthesized as an integrated site strategy.');

