  'Students learn that site is not background scenery; it is a set of physical, ecological, social, infrastructural, legal, and experiential forces that shape architecture. The course covers inventory and mapping, landform and accessible grading, water-sensitive design, living systems and planting, program and circulation, hardscape and outdoor comfort, urban and regional systems, regulation and feasibility, climate and equity, representation, and community, synthesized as an integrated site strategy.',
  $sitejson${"slug": "site-planning-and-landscape", "title": "Site Planning and Landscape", "description": "Students learn that site is not background scenery; it is a set of physical, ecological, social, infrastructural, legal, and experiential forces that shape architecture. The course covers inventory and mapping, landform and accessible grading, water-sensitive design, living systems and planting, program and circulation, hardscape and outdoor comfort, urban and regional systems, regulation and feasibility, climate and equity, representation, and community, synthesized as an integrated site strategy.", "topics": [{"id": "cf061be7-ac6f-45a6-bb17-a55dcb69ed58", "type": "topic", "title": "Site Planning as Architectural Groundwork: Observation, Scale, Context, and Design Intent", "description": "Students learn that site is not background scenery; it is a set of physical, ecological, social, infrastructural, legal, and experiential forces that shape architecture from the first sketch.", "children": [{"id": "e67a9e7a-aa09-4946-971f-a2ff363377c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site as active design agent", "children": [{"id": "3e6e1be5-758c-40af-91ad-888e5559f456", "type": "concept", "title": "Ground, climate, ecology, infrastructure, law, memory, and use"}, {"id": "71e37459-efb6-419c-b57b-233303e21b87", "type": "concept", "title": "Site response versus site imposition"}, {"id": "5cca9a89-3eea-497c-a02b-7ef92c4b6487", "type": "concept", "title": "Architecture, landscape, and urbanism as one system"}], "description": "Students learn to treat site conditions as generators of architecture, not limits to be added after the fact."}, {"id": "41b7c307-9613-4ea6-8493-9b91388c4ad3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Scales of site thinking", "children": [{"id": "d9777e84-6aa9-4afd-9e39-ae4a614dd56e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lot, block, district, watershed, corridor, city, and region"}, {"id": "28ea4922-6a47-4f7b-a346-2b33ba9f919f", "type": "concept", "title": "Immediate context and long-term transformation"}, {"id": "b10a6231-89cc-4b3c-a36f-28caa9e04e93", "type": "concept", "title": "Nested systems and design consequences"}], "description": "The point is to connect parcel-level decisions to neighborhood and regional systems."}, {"id": "95b6f464-310d-4c4e-8def-3c7d959d9d23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design intent from evidence", "children": [{"id": "853e029a-f98c-4a17-9ddf-a4181a333836", "type": "concept", "title": "Site questions, hypotheses, constraints, opportunities, and performance goals"}, {"id": "56f7f0b0-2900-4a6a-b95e-203559c3afa9", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-based concept development"}, {"id": "622be3ab-45f4-4c38-9203-ecc70021afb5", "type": "concept", "title": "From analysis to action"}], "description": "Students learn to derive design priorities from observable conditions."}]}, {"id": "5a279555-b85a-4a11-b483-cfe44be4afd9", "type": "topic", "title": "Site Inventory and Analysis: Fieldwork, Mapping, Climate, Context, Access, and Constraints", "description": "This module teaches students to gather, map, and interpret site evidence before making design claims.", "children": [{"id": "ff7f1f00-4af4-4d01-b6e8-8bd775ab6201", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field observation", "children": [{"id": "7547c5fe-f617-455b-bc8b-d4121796b165", "type": "concept", "title": "Photographs, sketches, measurements, sensory notes, use patterns, and time-of-day observations"}, {"id": "d040ab6f-4325-4d69-ac3d-40f0257a602d", "type": "concept", "title": "Weather, shade, noise, smell, wind, edges, and desire lines"}, {"id": "e33b01d4-e2ad-4283-85fb-1bf6179e6bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Field ethics and safety"}], "description": "Students practice direct site reading before abstract mapping."}, {"id": "059deff4-fb05-483e-8840-a37eba81c633", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mapping and layers", "children": [{"id": "524eecc6-fb6e-41f4-9445-105ddd738177", "type": "concept", "title": "Base maps, figure-ground, land use, access, hydrology, vegetation, utilities, and microclimate"}, {"id": "d808b648-ec96-4189-832e-ea11fd1868eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunities, constraints, and conflicts"}, {"id": "95f27913-aa77-4712-b764-b87c51e4e847", "type": "concept", "title": "Overlay analysis and hierarchy"}], "description": "The gist is to transform raw observations into legible site intelligence."}, {"id": "ad3abd10-6949-4414-9ed3-4b89d7865cc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Context interpretation", "children": [{"id": "06d71fff-2ecf-4c7e-a579-60bb5a44a447", "type": "concept", "title": "History, neighborhood form, mobility, demographics, ownership, and adjacent programs"}, {"id": "34098eac-e8ac-478f-ab3a-a6079fdcd2c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Views, landmarks, thresholds, and public/private gradients"}, {"id": "841354c7-30b6-4bfe-bde8-77bb5097a708", "type": "concept", "title": "Critical reading of assumptions"}], "description": "Students learn to connect site facts to design implications."}]}, {"id": "d94bd66f-9df4-4fbc-9c96-3fdde06da2b2", "type": "topic", "title": "Topography, Contours, Grading, Earthwork, Slopes, and Accessible Landform", "description": "Students learn how landform affects movement, drainage, cost, accessibility, foundations, views, and outdoor experience.", "children": [{"id": "48300b1d-ade3-428b-9250-0bf4f0171c91", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contour literacy", "children": [{"id": "bc1c634d-d0d7-4f62-a2e6-5cb0379faed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Contour intervals, spot elevations, slope percentages, ridges, valleys, high points, and low points"}, {"id": "c9d04adb-8fde-49a0-926d-a4eb54cf6ad1", "type": "concept", "title": "Cut, fill, retaining conditions, and drainage direction"}, {"id": "3f19e224-97d1-4bdd-85bd-59e6c63f5f18", "type": "concept", "title": "Sections as topographic evidence"}], "description": "Students learn to read and draw landform accurately."}, {"id": "e7d7489a-29eb-4139-823f-ef1084a5222c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Grading design", "children": [{"id": "8a5f2716-3ca3-4c07-9f72-b50f42327abf", "type": "concept", "title": "Pads, terraces, swales, berms, ramps, stairs, walls, and transitions"}, {"id": "73dba7ff-047e-47a0-848e-30b9239ce381", "type": "concept", "title": "Balancing earthwork and minimizing disturbance"}, {"id": "5db9fd82-3966-4f41-9e88-ce356ec78cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Grading plans and spot elevations"}], "description": "The point is to shape landform for use, drainage, constructability, and experience."}, {"id": "cfd80766-ec10-466e-9bf0-9b119f77dcbc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessible landform", "children": [{"id": "4257dbee-98ce-49d3-9c49-8d6179627a31", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible routes, cross slope, running slope, landings, curb ramps, handrails, and detectable warnings"}, {"id": "393b06e3-8e00-4661-97a0-1b69c155eed6", "type": "concept", "title": "Universal access through terrain"}, {"id": "cefcfab0-1ec4-42b1-b48a-994e96f04975", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding leftover accessibility paths"}], "description": "Students connect grading to inclusive movement."}]}, {"id": "609309c7-ef0c-4d41-80fa-82d5da56e550", "type": "topic", "title": "Hydrology, Stormwater, Green Infrastructure, Watersheds, and Water-Sensitive Design", "description": "This topic introduces water as a design system, from rainfall and runoff to infiltration, detention, water quality, and resilience.", "children": [{"id": "36769b21-13e4-4512-a81f-a2473bb0227e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Water movement", "children": [{"id": "97f89130-27bc-4187-bd43-c0d4d66ffebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Watersheds, subcatchments, runoff, infiltration, evapotranspiration, and groundwater"}, {"id": "14616733-6d8c-45a7-9570-39331ee6acee", "type": "concept", "title": "Impervious surfaces and time of concentration"}, {"id": "e0a47a64-0fad-4e3c-bc9b-11f78f5ecdd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Flooding, erosion, and downstream impacts"}], "description": "Students understand how water enters, crosses, and leaves a site."}, {"id": "177ee1bb-7ab1-438e-aac7-66b9f9f23fc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stormwater strategies", "children": [{"id": "8bda5b8f-ac28-48d9-a740-91d9c8f2ec79", "type": "concept", "title": "Bioswales, rain gardens, detention, retention, permeable paving, cisterns, green roofs, and constructed wetlands"}, {"id": "771478b6-7303-4634-9509-3581fcc12c4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Water quality and first flush"}, {"id": "b362296f-e720-46cd-a71c-454054a57ed3", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance and performance tradeoffs"}], "description": "The gist is to use water management as design structure."}, {"id": "7d546c41-2ebb-473b-bc08-ff5e035d7acc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resilience and regulation", "children": [{"id": "dcd9e647-240d-4ac3-9d66-c58b751fbe74", "type": "concept", "title": "Floodplains, storm events, sea-level rise, combined sewer overflow, and local stormwater ordinances"}, {"id": "f00c1329-ac06-43f4-b9d9-b34090c3e400", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-impact development and green infrastructure"}, {"id": "bdff8003-7a3a-482a-aa05-93f140f6167a", "type": "concept", "title": "Documenting stormwater concepts in design packages"}], "description": "Students connect hydrology to climate and approvals."}]}, {"id": "2bb09edc-aba1-43fa-89f6-2c949d0cdca5", "type": "topic", "title": "Ecology, Soils, Vegetation, Habitat, Planting Design, and Landscape Performance", "description": "Students study living systems as design material and performance infrastructure rather than decoration.", "children": [{"id": "7ea9e89a-af12-4127-a84e-86c49d7aded4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Soils and living systems", "children": [{"id": "5c1ade35-ac96-4a85-8ee6-fb6c7a623d80", "type": "concept", "title": "Soil texture, compaction, drainage, organic matter, contamination, and remediation"}, {"id": "c5b10ba1-e15a-4eaa-94e7-653ed44d39f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Root zones, soil volumes, and urban soil constraints"}, {"id": "ad271f05-e432-48d4-872d-55fb66e6d562", "type": "concept", "title": "Testing and interpretation"}], "description": "Students learn that soil is infrastructure for plants, water, carbon, and habitat."}, {"id": "b52a9a2f-57a2-4728-b685-54fb3bdcfee0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planting design", "children": [{"id": "903a9187-5a56-481d-ac84-4d98855fdbae", "type": "concept", "title": "Native/adapted plants, canopy, understory, groundcover, seasonality, succession, and maintenance"}, {"id": "0edd1c7e-7d3f-48f2-9a1e-86a8a4b6b5e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Biodiversity, habitat, pollinators, and invasive species"}, {"id": "50f9560f-7f8d-43de-8b77-636abba6ba48", "type": "concept", "title": "Planting plans and schedules"}], "description": "The point is to choose vegetation for ecological function, climate fit, and spatial experience."}, {"id": "1dc71ad4-8d68-4f89-b8df-3d5ece05d6e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Landscape performance", "children": [{"id": "7c41d913-0fec-45f7-a7a3-de5624fdb456", "type": "concept", "title": "Shade, heat reduction, stormwater capture, carbon, habitat, health, and social use"}, {"id": "bdeced8c-5f63-4480-a455-58a2fe875d8f", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance metrics and case-study evidence"}, {"id": "0e9f46ae-d0dd-4250-86ef-dcd9753a3644", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-occupancy evaluation"}], "description": "Students learn to measure landscape benefits."}]}, {"id": "fd13411c-a0d3-48b6-a7dd-b2ec9d89fd3d", "type": "topic", "title": "Site Planning Principles: Program, Adjacency, Circulation, Thresholds, and Spatial Organization", "description": "This module connects building program to exterior rooms, movement systems, arrival sequences, service access, and site logic.", "children": [{"id": "c41a16f9-60eb-445a-a873-a991a1f04ec3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Program on site", "children": [{"id": "9ae1d9f6-7522-4a96-9118-4a4b31c7a712", "type": "concept", "title": "Entries, service, outdoor rooms, event areas, parking, drop-off, storage, and support spaces"}, {"id": "9a375550-4e0d-42