": "Concrete, asphalt, unit pavers, gravel, decking, permeable paving, and stabilized surfaces"}, {"id": "58da9fc9-f5e8-4ed0-ae62-71eb30d1a26a", "type": "concept", "title": "Slip resistance, accessibility, joints, drainage, and durability"}, {"id": "64816f3c-13e7-4202-bdb0-e47fa86d4782", "type": "concept", "title": "Material life cycle and repair"}], "description": "Students learn how hardscape affects movement, water, heat, maintenance, and character."}, {"id": "30e19833-ecd6-4ebc-a66a-e2bd3c743959", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Site elements and details", "children": [{"id": "6c1f15de-4da3-4dd9-8eab-c316fe8a0546", "type": "concept", "title": "Walls, curbs, stairs, ramps, railings, benches, bollards, bike racks, planters, and trash/recycling"}, {"id": "c356dde3-6e66-4a7b-86c5-4c3450d58c23", "type": "concept", "title": "Details, tolerances, edges, and constructability"}, {"id": "a6d188da-9a5a-4fed-b459-ef1401ee5c87", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordination with civil and landscape drawings"}], "description": "The point is to make outdoor spaces usable and buildable."}, {"id": "ead6adaa-fa96-4eb7-9df7-fb88cac9658b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lighting and safety", "children": [{"id": "97b67a6f-fc49-4857-aeb7-5fc49d8e145c", "type": "concept", "title": "Pedestrian lighting, glare, dark sky, security, wayfinding, and energy"}, {"id": "d5bfbe96-62d0-4fb1-9e02-8c3d7b28ba65", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting levels and fixture selection"}, {"id": "dfec65bb-b8e8-419e-8eef-53d8cf315536", "type": "concept", "title": "Crime prevention through environmental design"}], "description": "Students connect nighttime use to comfort, safety, and ecology."}]}, {"id": "432093f4-4426-40b9-948f-c36d61e90a44", "type": "topic", "title": "Outdoor Space Design: Human Comfort, Microclimate, Views, Sequence, Safety, and Everyday Use", "description": "This topic focuses on the experience of people using outdoor rooms in different seasons, times of day, and social conditions.", "children": [{"id": "7e4ec7cc-fac9-46d1-a5ff-28c399263042", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Microclimate and comfort", "children": [{"id": "727aa96c-2cb6-4b15-adbe-3dfad386e4da", "type": "concept", "title": "Sun, shade, wind, humidity, thermal comfort, seasonal change, and shelter"}, {"id": "cc90dbcd-12c9-4ad8-9958-6cef1a92ea51", "type": "concept", "title": "Trees, canopies, walls, water, and material albedo"}, {"id": "d03f3ff0-f779-44ae-8b96-4ac1df94489e", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat mitigation and cold-climate comfort"}], "description": "Students learn to design for bodies in weather."}, {"id": "a4c5e33c-30eb-4f0c-8b6b-cd077744f97e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experience and sequence", "children": [{"id": "225ef3d5-7a6e-4fc5-9d20-d2163500da71", "type": "concept", "title": "Arrival, compression/release, framed views, prospect/refuge, sound, smell, texture, and movement"}, {"id": "70ea61b2-694a-42e3-b8fd-afe3d37f2bc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Edges, centers, thresholds, and destinations"}, {"id": "83b6fe42-b6e3-4bf7-8e73-7bab80e7fca6", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative without over-designing"}], "description": "The gist is to make outdoor space memorable and legible."}, {"id": "e11b5bdf-abaf-484f-94f1-ba4ded8133d3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social use and safety", "children": [{"id": "0949da9b-1561-4ad3-b315-2ec5f662870f", "type": "concept", "title": "Seating choice, visibility, inclusivity, play, gathering, rest, and informal use"}, {"id": "eb99fd40-462c-43cb-bd91-58f2d38f0e04", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance, surveillance, lighting, and stewardship"}, {"id": "58703f26-6b2e-4166-8066-19c5f91ab692", "type": "concept", "title": "Comfort across age, ability, and culture"}], "description": "Students design outdoor spaces that support everyday life."}]}, {"id": "7bec144e-3c74-4d21-9e05-1e6353b4fb23", "type": "topic", "title": "Urban Site Design: Streets, Blocks, Public Realm, Edges, Mixed Use, and Neighborhood Context", "description": "Students study sites as parts of larger urban systems, including streets, blocks, frontages, public space, and land-use patterns.", "children": [{"id": "c6efe687-b4a0-482b-9d58-c9c34c571c29", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Urban morphology", "children": [{"id": "8033145b-055c-4c81-9c7d-95daa334395a", "type": "concept", "title": "Blocks, parcels, streets, alleys, frontages, setbacks, landmarks, and open-space networks"}, {"id": "5a1f70eb-0d46-43b5-9db5-c5f4d9f4106d", "type": "concept", "title": "Density, grain, scale, and building typologies"}, {"id": "8c41d312-5661-47f6-a271-340d3b6a2f10", "type": "concept", "title": "Historic and contemporary patterns"}], "description": "Students learn to read the shape of cities around a site."}, {"id": "e7ecc9eb-205b-414a-9fb5-ec9ced2d4382", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public realm design", "children": [{"id": "a931a8f2-9ac3-48c3-a7e7-69340139e94a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sidewalks, plazas, parks, transit stops, bike networks, street trees, and curb uses"}, {"id": "a1bac122-3f5f-4016-809b-d7a7e1909ffa", "type": "concept", "title": "Active edges, transparency, accessibility, and seating"}, {"id": "0f8628ab-a9fd-4041-b736-90bf81f346e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Public/private responsibility and maintenance"}], "description": "The point is to understand streets and open spaces as shared civic infrastructure."}, {"id": "9c6a3bf8-475d-43c6-8ddd-bae948c04517", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mixed-use relationships", "children": [{"id": "21019c6c-4f8a-4c6f-9931-5ce4d4bca16e", "type": "concept", "title": "Ground-floor uses, loading, parking, housing, retail, institutions, and community facilities"}, {"id": "33ef2233-09d0-403e-9075-5e8635a58514", "type": "concept", "title": "Noise, privacy, security, and service access"}, {"id": "62c0f757-fe47-4add-a7d0-8d8a1f0d3698", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban design guidelines and placemaking"}], "description": "Students coordinate site design with urban program and neighborhood life."}]}, {"id": "023ae9b1-84f0-4093-a6a0-ebeae6b38d55", "type": "topic", "title": "Landscape Systems, Infrastructure, Mobility, Service Networks, and Regional Scales", "description": "This module expands site planning beyond the parcel to ecological, infrastructural, metropolitan, and regional relationships.", "children": [{"id": "3d3abca5-9fd8-4464-8929-df71d2c7cef9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure as landscape", "children": [{"id": "6cfa9d3e-91fd-41d8-9657-3f280fe8cd88", "type": "concept", "title": "Roads, utilities, stormwater, transit, rail, ports, energy, and digital networks"}, {"id": "3bcbfebf-ff37-4ec5-9d74-2ce168340f2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Visible and invisible systems"}, {"id": "4221f608-029b-4d89-9594-61a7aa24e481", "type": "concept", "title": "Infrastructure corridors as public realm and habitat"}], "description": "Students learn to see infrastructure as spatial and ecological design material."}, {"id": "71b8128b-45cc-481e-a0af-5780e46d0e23", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mobility networks", "children": [{"id": "b2aa6b35-e61b-4070-a5ae-97b84d5c7806", "type": "concept", "title": "Walking, cycling, transit, vehicles, service, emergency access, and micromobility"}, {"id": "c51a5b95-1d5e-457d-bca8-e70737d36931", "type": "concept", "title": "First/last-mile connections"}, {"id": "47dbc299-abb2-4f15-9714-51edcaf79ed8", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, equity, and mode shift"}], "description": "The gist is to connect site access to larger movement systems."}, {"id": "26827917-c5df-4c65-9670-26b1cefb42dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regional systems", "children": [{"id": "8c4eca01-fb53-4387-b0b0-f5306275ebc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Greenways, blueways, food systems, heat islands, ecological corridors, and regional growth"}, {"id": "3415c0f5-756c-42ec-b7d0-53cf881e97a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Metropolitan scale and rural/urban edge"}, {"id": "0a486e38-2714-4063-8ac8-c562ee0cda06", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning"}], "description": "Students broaden site thinking to watershed, habitat, economy, and settlement patterns."}]}, {"id": "2256459d-70ca-421a-937a-fe3a6977159e", "type": "topic", "title": "Zoning, Land Use, Entitlements, Codes, Easements, Utilities, and Development Feasibility", "description": "Students learn the regulatory and practical controls that affect what can be built, where, and under what approvals.", "children": [{"id": "414d4613-9854-40ce-ae23-5e3300258cd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulatory framework", "children": [{"id": "d12feb92-8445-4bd2-8194-38cefe1a4733", "type": "concept", "title": "Zoning district, use, setbacks, height, FAR, lot coverage, parking, loading, signage, and landscaping requirements"}, {"id": "ab8150bb-e30a-4d93-a035-cdba447d1acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Overlays, design review, and special districts"}, {"id": "1f61a76c-9d13-4e42-86bf-c1fab08cab8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Entitlements, variances, and approvals"}], "description": "Students learn the controls that shape buildable site strategy."}, {"id": "4692cffc-f0a3-4c5b-b18d-8537455d6376", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Property and utilities", "children": [{"id": "620ffe08-8946-4124-8c9d-176d6efb5540", "type": "concept", "title": "Property lines, easements, rights-of-way, setbacks, utilities, service corridors, and access agreements"}, {"id": "c629de6b-4c05-45b7-ba8a-3febc383f9f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Survey, title, and civil coordination"}, {"id": "adc62068-0f03-4963-95e4-432e35deb11f", "type": "concept", "title": "Utility capacity and relocation"}], "description": "The point is to identify hidden constraints before design decisions harden."}, {"id": "9e80f79a-2013-4884-8337-8a640bfd57ff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Feasibility and risk", "children": [{"id": "706d6dec-7b47-4b01-a026-2ae91cfa6cac", "type": "concept", "title": "Development yield, phasing, cost, constructability, permitting schedule, and stakeholder risk"}, {"id": "f47a4807-933e-45c2-83eb-a23a3ee166de", "type": "concept", "title": "Environmental review and community review"}, {"id": "66f2bf91-4801-4583-8a3e-2325787a167d", "type": "concept", "title": "Feasibility matrices and decision logs"}], "description": "Students connect site planning to project viability."}]}, {"id": "ad602fd0-7a10-4343-8666-336b3fee8ce2", "type": "topic", "title": "Sustainable Site Design: Heat, Carbon, Biodiversity, Resilience, Equity, and Climate Adaptation", "description": "This topic integrates sustainable design goals with measurable performance, climate risk, public health, and social value.", "children": [{"id": "17136a69-494c-4017-abaa-58cd848f4a37", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Climate adaptation", "children": [{"id": "7c4ff9a1-c1a1-46a4-bfd1-0ebd2032249d", "type": "concept", "title": "Extreme heat, flooding, drought, wildfire, storms, sea-level rise, and air quality"}, {"id": "92742b27-5f6b-42ad-ba91-b7d1174a516c", "type": "concept", "title": "Redundancy, refuge, shade, drainage, and emergency access"}, {"id": "fb1650e3-db6d-427c-9563-780eeae94ae2", "type": "concept", "title": "Adaptation strategies at parcel and district scales"}], "description": "Students learn to design sites for changing risk conditions."}, {"id": "b98c9335-3d64-4735-a18a-a7ee910a9b04", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Low-carbon site design", "children": [{"id": "988aacfb-d34e-444a-8982-0aa5e4661ec4", "type": "concept", "title": "Earthwork minimization, material reuse, low-carbon paving, tree preservation, and soil carbon"}, {"id": "21785289-0d04-4ce4-9173-9235ede933fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Construction disturbance and lifecycle thinking"}, {"id": "09849ebf-ee40-47d5-81ca-7d317f1ac443", "type": "concept", "title": "Landscape maintenance emissions"}], "description": "The gist is to reduce embodied and operational impacts of site work."}, {"id": "32222d55-90b5-4554-845d-95108bb07e67", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equity and environmental justice", "children": [{"id": "31ca2dc2-3257-4671-aa0e-b96f124c54b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Access to shade, parks, mobility, clean water, safety, and public amenities"}, {"id": "dd27f666-17c9-4d89-a4d3-2ba946f3db65", "type": "concept", "title": "Heat-vulnerable populations and historic disinvestment"}, {"id": "3d0dfa3d-0df6-4614-904b-96cef66ad2bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Community benefits and anti-displacement awareness"}], "description": "Students connect sustainability to people and power."}]}, {"id": "c70e870d-caca-4569-b2df-156f9187ea8c", "type": "topic", "title": "Representation and Digital Site Tools: Survey, GIS, Diagrams, Models, Sections, and Performance Metrics", "description": "Students learn to communicate site intelligence through maps, diagrams, drawings, models, and evidence-based metrics.", "children": [{"id": "aa7ca87c-7f11-40ca-a3d3-4f9518f83ff1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Survey and base data", "children": [{"id": "10042328-f91f-4def-864f-0dacbf0adeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Topographic surveys, GIS layers, aerial imagery, LiDAR, soil maps, flood maps, and census data"}, {"id": "bf587ba7-78c9-445d-bd88-dd0536d8b91d", "type": "concept", "title": "Datum, scale, accuracy, and source reliability"}, {"id": "ec63f3b9-3255-4907-86ba-d874878cca62", "type": "concept", "title": "Data cleaning and attribution"}], "description": "Students learn to work from reliable site information."}, {"id": "ccbee760-e46f-4710-ad74-6b6561d2e043", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drawings and diagrams", "children": [{"id": "0b06a4fc-11b7-47ea-8faa-6e2bb7655fee", "type": "concept", "title": "Maps, sections, axonometrics, slope diagrams, sun/wind diagrams, hydrology diagrams, and circulation diagrams"}, {"id": "ff1af2f2-6c3f-4e6e-b49a-0730f011b742", "type": "concept", "title": "Graphic hierarchy and annotation"}, {"id": "b1085c40-435a-416d-bcb3-629b2435a632", "type": "concept", "title": "From analysis drawing to design drawing"}], "description": "The point is to communicate site logic clearly."}, {"id": "a7bd4b10-86d9-48ff-ae85-04869b3bec7e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Models and metrics", "children": [{"id": "9c7c3433-24c8-4f47-b79d-0a57bbe188b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical models, digital terrain models, massing models, GIS, daylight/shadow studies, stormwater estimates, and landscape-performance metrics"}, {"id": "f1134f17-fcab-4a3b-a677-261fa8ca1bc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Iteration and evidence"}, {"id": "00c0e45f-8f68-410e-8faf-9c7bee56f046", "type": "concept", "title": "Limitations of simulation"}], "description": "Students use tools to test rather than merely illustrate."}]}, {"id": "1fa020c9-d5d3-4bfc-ad03-2f41d4887820", "type": "topic", "title": "Site as Program and Community: Stakeholders, Public Life, Cultural Landscape, and Participatory Design", "description": "This module treats site as social and cultural territory shaped by communities, histories, use patterns, memory, and power.", "children": [{"id": "15c2e83c-6d9a-4aad-ae90-486f5f9a78c2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Stakeholders and users", "children": [{"id": "9ade4ab3-7d13-4e55-9bc3-10b8beacc3cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Residents, workers, visitors, owners, agencies, maintenance staff, and marginalized users"}, {"id": "11378073-d1af-4a89-8a86-002a245f12b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Interviews, observation, workshops, and surveys"}, {"id": "33bc68ff-0cb5-4835-9faf-da0e2c9351ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation, consent, and interpretation"}], "description": "Students learn whose site knowledge matters."}, {"id": "54fd527e-187d-4296-942d-64582c7d2ccc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cultural landscape", "children": [{"id": "0a481017-dac8-4a3f-a5dc-b2b917a22ccf", "type": "concept", "title": "Historic layers, rituals, public art, informal uses, indigenous histories, and contested narratives"}, {"id": "cdc0b675-a1ca-4d27-8fad-23e5144761df", "type": "concept", "title": "Preservation, adaptation, and interpretation"}, {"id": "14e5174c-543a-47db-aa46-eca8034d4de3", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding erasure through design"}], "description": "The gist is to see sites as carriers of memory and identity."}, {"id": "68259f86-fdc8-4cc6-8670-509f97f2320f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participation and stewardship", "children": [{"id": "37b3c922-ea11-425e-8791-4fa0f7792092", "type": "concept", "title": "Co-design, maintenance partnerships, programming, governance, and community stewardship"}, {"id": "1dbef02c-e519-4fcb-b17a-e1a900fb8b45", "type": "concept", "title": "Temporary activation and tactical urbanism"}, {"id": "7746f754-2a1e-4592-b08e-47e019f86bc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Measuring social value"}], "description": "Students connect design to long-term care and public life."}]}, {"id": "868a5e05-02b5-4423-9729-745fa5594916", "type": "topic", "title": "Integrated Site Strategy Capstone: From Analysis to Landscape-Architectural Design Proposal", "description": "Students synthesize the course by producing a site strategy and design proposal that connects analysis, ecology, access, program, and architectural intent.", "children": [{"id": "41498213-c3b0-4e9b-8b06-301ce2c67471", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research synthesis", "children": [{"id": "8deaa81c-e15b-4eda-a4ca-1d416dfccc80", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory atlas, constraints/opportunities, stakeholder findings, regulatory matrix, and performance goals"}, {"id": "67ef28d3-af78-4fd6-9ea5-1a047d850c78", "type": "concept", "title": "Design priorities and tradeoffs"}, {"id": "fbacd725-6b89-4634-b9a5-8687f7fd2ae5", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept statement and criteria"}], "description": "Students turn all site evidence into a clear design argument."}, {"id": "55417b4b-8256-44c3-9544-c91d01408fa8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Design proposal", "children": [{"id": "769da754-9e32-4717-8efe-8faa3a4b5d1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Site plan, grading concept, stormwater strategy, planting concept, hardscape, circulation, and outdoor rooms"}, {"id": "9202cad6-f631-40b9-ab46-96b3c19d8796", "type": "concept", "title": "Architecture-ground relationship"}, {"id": "a0bb68d1-d3ba-485e-979f-d34c61e26f5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Phasing and constructability"}], "description": "The point is to integrate building, landscape, ecology, and access."}, {"id": "fc248398-d056-4a01-8d13-33fbe4b6a010", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Final communication package", "children": [{"id": "d1c3b68b-cb03-48b9-abd2-a1bd14e84240", "type": "concept", "title": "Plans, sections, diagrams, precedent references, material palette, metrics, and narrative"}, {"id": "efc04967-9099-4e25-9f9b-00fff99da10e", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique response and revision"}, {"id": "9909c64c-c5da-45a3-a3b1-77ea193d36c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio-ready presentation"}], "description": "Students produce a review-ready set of deliverables."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$sitejson$::jsonb,
